    {
      "id": "french",
      "name": "French",
      "colour": "#2f4d8f",
      "brief": "Let his left go. He is marching it off the plateau in front of you to get round your right, and every battalion that leaves the crest leaves it emptier — so the longer Legrand holds Sokolnitz with far too little, the better the trade. What you have in the bottom is two divisions nobody up there can see. Everything you do is uphill and costs Fatigue before it costs anything else, so do not halt on the slope: that is where their guns reach and where your columns are deepest. You have about an hour before their Guard comes round the far side of the plateau.",
