      "deploymentZone": [100, 100, 720, 1060]
    },
    {
      "id": "allied",
      "name": "Russo-Austrian",
      "colour": "#e3e7ef",
      "brief": "The plan is four days old and it is to turn the French right at Sokolnitz, which is thin, which is the whole reason it is the plan. Your left is already on its way there and it is walking off the plateau to go. What is left in the centre is Kollowrat's column, strung out along the crest in the order it was marching in and facing the wrong way for anything coming up the western slope. That crest is also the road home for everything below it. The Guard is behind Krzenowitz and will take twenty minutes to reach the high ground: decide before then whether you are still turning his right or getting your centre back.",
